# Cloudflare Pages reads this file. The project is set up there with no
# framework preset, no build command, and / as the output directory, so a push
# to main deploys the repo as it stands.
# Two kinds of rule live here: 200 rewrites that keep a published URL working
# after the file behind it moved, and 301s for pages and files that were
# retired or renamed.

# ---- moved in the repo, not on the web ----------------------------------
# The pages live under pages/ now, and the icons and documents under files/.
# A 200 is a rewrite, not a redirect: the address bar keeps the short URL and
# Cloudflare serves the file from its new path.
#
# Every target here is a directory, never a path ending in index.html. Pages
# canonicalizes a URL that names index.html (and one that ends .html) by
# redirecting to the directory, and it does that to the target of a rewrite as
# well, which turns the rewrite into a visible 307 and leaks the long path into
# the address bar. A directory is already canonical, so it is served as-is.
# The splat covers the slashed form, /tiny/ with an empty splat.
#
# The bare form is sent on to the slashed one rather than served. Served at
# /cosmos, the tool's relative links resolved against / and all 404ed, and
# every page is better off with one address.
/crucible        /crucible/                       301
/crucible/*      /pages/projects/crucible/:splat  200

/tiny            /tiny/                           301
/tiny/*          /pages/projects/tiny/:splat      200

/cosmos          /cosmos/                         301
/cosmos/*        /pages/projects/cosmos/:splat    200

# GoDash's subpages are published without a trailing slash (/godash/privacy),
# so they are privacy.html and contact.html rather than directories. Pages
# serves a .html file at its bare name, which is what the splat hands it. As
# directories they were the long-path 307 described above: the bare name of a
# directory is not canonical, the slashed one is.
/godash          /godash/                         301
/godash/*        /pages/projects/godash/:splat    200

/misc            /misc/                           301
/misc/*          /pages/misc/:splat               200

# The old file URLs. Every page here points at the new paths already; these are
# for links that left the site: the resume URL in particular is on a CV and in
# applications, and the preview image is cached by anything that has scraped a
# link to the site.
/favicon.svg                               /files/images/favicon.svg                  301
/favicon.png                               /files/images/favicon.png                  301
/og.png                                    /files/images/og.png                       301
/files/matthew-saunders-resume.pdf         /files/docs/matthew-saunders-resume.pdf    301
/files/fundamentals-of-remote-sensing.pdf  /files/docs/fundamentals-of-remote-sensing.pdf  301

# ---- retired pages -------------------------------------------------------
# The two pages folded into /misc/. Both were live and indexed, so they redirect
# rather than 404.
/hobbies    /misc/  301
/hobbies/*  /misc/  301
/gallery    /misc/  301
/gallery/*  /misc/  301

# The projects are entries on the home page now, linking to their own pages;
# nothing lives under /projects/ any more. The index and all three writeups
# were live and indexed, so the whole tree redirects home.
/projects/*  /  301
/projects  /  301
